### TITLE ###
EchoNoneRendersNothingAndRepeatsItself
### DESCRIPTION ###
The whole point of this mode: read FRAMES and confirm the value appears in none
of them, while VALUE shows it still reached the caller. Every frame is identical
because rendering anything that varied - even a length - would leak the secret
to someone watching the screen.
### PROMPT ###
Password >
### ECHO ###
none
### KEYS ###
"hunter2"
enter
### VALUE ###
hunter2
### FRAMES ###
--- frame 0 (initial) ---
Password >█
--- frame 1 (h) ---
Password >█
--- frame 2 (u) ---
Password >█
--- frame 3 (n) ---
Password >█
--- frame 4 (t) ---
Password >█
--- frame 5 (e) ---
Password >█
--- frame 6 (r) ---
Password >█
--- frame 7 (2) ---
Password >█

### TITLE ###
EchoNoneFreezesTheCursorButKeepsBackspace
### DESCRIPTION ###
Left and Home are no-ops in secret mode - there is no visible cursor to move, so
honouring them would edit a position the user cannot see. Backspace still drops
the last rune, which is the one edit that needs no visible position.
### PROMPT ###
>
### ECHO ###
none
### KEYS ###
"ab"
left
home
backspace
enter
### VALUE ###
a
### FRAMES ###
--- frame 0 (initial) ---
>█
--- frame 1 (a) ---
>█
--- frame 2 (b) ---
>█
--- frame 3 (left) ---
>█
--- frame 4 (home) ---
>█
--- frame 5 (backspace) ---
>█

### TITLE ###
EchoMaskedShowsOneDotPerRune
### DESCRIPTION ###
Masked mode reveals the length and nothing else.
### PROMPT ###
>
### ECHO ###
masked
### KEYS ###
"abc"
enter
### VALUE ###
abc
### FRAMES ###
--- frame 0 (initial) ---
>█
--- frame 1 (a) ---
>•█
--- frame 2 (b) ---
>••█
--- frame 3 (c) ---
>•••█
--- frame 4 (enter) ---
>•••

### TITLE ###
MaskedSummaryDoesNotLeak
### DESCRIPTION ###
The collapsed summary is the frame that outlives the prompt in a scrollback
buffer, so it must not print what the field spent the whole session hiding.
### PROMPT ###
pw >
### ECHO ###
masked
### KEYS ###
"sec"
enter
### VALUE ###
sec
### FRAMES ###
--- frame 0 (initial) ---
pw >█
--- frame 1 (s) ---
pw >•█
--- frame 2 (e) ---
pw >••█
--- frame 3 (c) ---
pw >•••█
--- frame 4 (enter) ---
pw >•••
